Align nil's builtins doc fixtures with Lix's documentation.

Under the Lix overlay, nil links Lix (not upstream CppNix) and generates its
builtins database from it. Lix documents some builtins with complexity notes
that upstream CppNix does not have, so nil's hardcoded expected doc strings no
longer match: `builtins.attrNames` gained "O(l n log n)" (breaking
`crates/builtin` `tests::sanity`), and `builtins.head` gained "Has constant
time complexity." (breaking the `ide::hover` `builtin_with`/`builtin_alias`
expect-tests).

We deliberately keep the tests enabled (they catch breakage in the Lix builtins
dump) and instead update the fixtures to Lix's current strings. This patch is
intentionally tightly coupled: if Lix changes these docs, or nil's source moves,
it will fail loudly on the next upgrade, which is the intended signal.

--- a/crates/builtin/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/builtin/src/lib.rs
@@ -47,7 +47,9 @@
                     "\
 Return the names of the attributes in the set *set* in an
 alphabetically sorted list. For instance, `builtins.attrNames { y
-= 1; x = \"foo\"; }` evaluates to `[ \"x\" \"y\" ]`.\
+= 1; x = \"foo\"; }` evaluates to `[ \"x\" \"y\" ]`.
+
+Has `O(l n log n)` time complexity, where `n` is number of attributes in the *set* and `l` is the maximum attribute name length.\
                 "
                 ),
                 impure_only: false,
--- a/crates/ide/src/ide/hover.rs
+++ b/crates/ide/src/ide/hover.rs
@@ -387,6 +387,8 @@
                 Return the first element of a list; abort evaluation if the argument
                 isn’t a list or is an empty list. You can test whether a list is
                 empty by comparing it with `[]`.
+
+                Has constant time complexity.
             "#]],
         );
     }
@@ -404,6 +406,8 @@
                 Return the first element of a list; abort evaluation if the argument
                 isn’t a list or is an empty list. You can test whether a list is
                 empty by comparing it with `[]`.
+
+                Has constant time complexity.
             "#]],
         );
     }
